## Build, run, and test

```bash
make run         # run the application
make test        # run the test suite
make test-cover  # run tests and open an HTML coverage report
make fix         # apply Go 1.26 modernizers (go fix)
make fix-check   # preview modernizer fixes without applying (go fix -diff)
```

Configuration comes from environment variables loaded from `.env` (see that file for the keys this project expects).

## Conventions
- Keep everything under `internal/core/**` free of framework, database, and HTTP imports.
- Adapters translate between the outside world and domain types; they hold no business rules.
- Co-locate tests (`*_test.go`); the service layer is unit-tested against the in-memory mock repository.
- Run `gofmt`, `go vet ./...`, and `go fix ./...` (Go 1.26 modernizers; preview with `make fix-check`) before committing.
